# --- the match is live; sweep the camera the full width, both ways ---
#
# sdb_pan alternates direction every 24 frames, which is ~150 px of travel:
# enough to carry a player across the screen edge and back, but never enough
# to carry one from one edge of the 512-pixel world to the other. The artifacts
# this vector exists to catch are boundary artifacts -- a sprite clipped a
# column short, one part landing a pixel from the next, a stale part held in the
# overscan band -- and they only show once a character has walked the whole
# distance rather than stepped across the boundary once.
#
# So: 72-frame holds, alternating. That is ~450 px of travel per direction at
# the 6-7 px per frame the game scrolls (docs/research.md 24), which is the
# width of the world. Directions alternate so every object crosses both edges
# on the way in and on the way out, which is the only way a one-sided artifact
# cannot hide.
#
# Format: one "<frame> <BUTTONS>" line per state change, absolute state
# ("-" is release). `#` starts a comment.

